02:40:16.320 --> 02:40:21.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, pero essentially, ang intindi ko sa inyo, yung ibang mga proyektong nakalista na ngayon, papalitan.

asr-002751
02:40:22.060 --> 02:40:22.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ganun po ba?

asr-002752
02:40:23.200 --> 02:40:31.560
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: Mayroong mga projects na hindi naman papalitan, siguro i-reduce lang nila yung amount.

asr-002753
02:40:32.120 --> 02:40:34.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, i-reduce ang amount, no?

asr-002754
02:40:34.380 --> 02:40:44.560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, in other words, I am expecting that the list of projects under all the programs of DPDL, there will be changes, no?

asr-002755
02:40:45.280 --> 02:40:46.420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ito na ngayon ang question.

asr-002756
02:40:46.420 --> 02:40:51.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sabi nyo, yung NEP, yung mga, bawat proyekto na nasa NEP, ay,

asr-002757
02:40:51.340 --> 02:40:52.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: dumaan sa RDC.

asr-002758
02:40:53.720 --> 02:40:57.760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ngayon, meron kayong ipapasok na bago, worth 20 billion.

asr-002759
02:40:58.560 --> 02:41:02.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi biro, ang pagbabago na yan, e, dumaan pa rin ba yan sa RDC?

asr-002760
02:41:03.320 --> 02:41:06.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Meron pa rin ba yan, vetting, etc., etc.?

asr-002761
02:41:06.220 --> 02:41:10.880
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: Your Honorable Interpolator, the same requirement.

asr-002762
02:41:11.560 --> 02:41:12.660
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: The same requirement.

asr-002763
02:41:12.900 --> 02:41:20.440
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: If they pass the same compliance of the requirements, ipapasok nila doon sa kanilang institutional amendments.

asr-002764
02:41:21.340 --> 02:41:24.340
Deputy Speaker Raymond Democrito C. Mendoza: With your kind indulgence, Congressman Tino.

asr-002765
02:41:25.880 --> 02:41:26.560
Deputy Speaker Raymond Democrito C. Mendoza: Motion?

asr-002766
02:41:26.940 --> 02:41:27.820
Deputy Speaker Raymond Democrito C. Mendoza: Majority Leader, please.

asr-002767
02:41:29.420 --> 02:41:30.120
Deputy Speaker Raymond Democrito C. Mendoza: Majority Leader.

asr-002768
02:41:32.300 --> 02:41:33.460
Deputy Speaker Raymond Democrito C. Mendoza: Session suspended.

asr-002777
02:42:33.660 --> 02:42:46.420
Deputy Speaker Raymond Democrito C. Mendoza: Session resumed. Majority Leader, please. Majority Leader?

asr-002777-split-2
02:42:46.420 --> 02:42:49.860
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Mr. Speaker, I move that we recognize the sponsor.

asr-002778
02:42:49.880 --> 02:43:04.260
Deputy Speaker Raymond Democrito C. Mendoza: Recognize the sponsor. Mr. Sponsor, you're recognized. And our Congressman for his interpellation, Representative Tinio was interpellating. Our apologies, sir, please proceed.

asr-002778-split-2
02:43:04.260 --> 02:43:19.860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you. So, Mr. Speaker, nagpapasalamat po ako doon sa commitment ng sponsor na ibigay yung proposed institutional amendments para mapag-aralan po.

asr-002779
02:43:19.880 --> 02:43:34.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Ngayon, siguro ito na ang pinakamahalagang punto. Kanina, sabi nyo, you assured na wala nang allocables, wala nang leadership, no?

asr-002780
02:43:34.200 --> 02:43:49.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ibig po ba inyo sabihin na sa kasalukuyang budget for 2027 ay wala nang listahan ng mga proyekto na isinusumite ang mga kongreses?

asr-002781
02:43:49.880 --> 02:43:57.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At hindi ba yan ang listahan na bumubuo sa institutional amendments na inyong ipapasok?

asr-002782
02:43:58.500 --> 02:44:06.880
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: Wala dahil, una, kailangan ho yung requirements. Kaya nga, nilagyan nila ng mga requirements na mahirap i-comply.

asr-002783
02:44:07.440 --> 02:44:15.660
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: Dahil kailangan, bago nila tanggapin yung mga proposals mo, ay kailangan mo na i-comply mong lahat ng requirements as needed by the department.

asr-002784
02:44:15.660 --> 02:44:17.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kung may requirements, tatanggapin?

asr-002785
02:44:18.200 --> 02:44:19.580
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: I do not know.

asr-002786
02:44:19.880 --> 02:44:28.920
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: May time pa, Your Honor, Mr. Speaker. Dahil maigsin ang panahon, mahirap i-comply ang lahat ng requirements.

asr-002787
02:44:29.400 --> 02:44:45.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, alam naman po natin sa House na meron talagang mga listahan dahil may mga deadline na pinapaabot sa mga opisina na mag-submit kayo ng inyong listahan by a certain time.

asr-002788
02:44:45.460 --> 02:44:49.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, this includes the projects under the...

asr-002789
02:44:49.880 --> 02:45:01.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So meron po yan. Ngayon, kaugnay nito, nais kong suportahan yung kaninang panawagan ni Representative Tiangco

asr-002790
02:45:01.640 --> 02:45:21.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: for 2026. And in fact, extend it as well to the 2025, 2024, and 2023 budget. Dahil po, sinabi ni Secretary Bonoan, siya nagsabi, siya nakakaalam, siya ang sekretary nun, hawak niya ang budget,

asr-002791
02:45:21.440 --> 02:45:37.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sinabi niya sa Sandigang Bayan na meron pong allocables ang mga kongresista, baseline 500 million for district, and 130 million per party list representative.

asr-002792
02:45:37.840 --> 02:45:44.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa kanya nang galing yun. At sworn testimony niya yun, so yan na nga po ang totoo.

asr-002793
02:45:44.820 --> 02:45:51.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And this may be confirmed by the independent...

asr-002794
02:45:51.440 --> 02:46:04.660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: independent research of investigative media. So may mga listahan na po, for example, sa PCIJ, na naglabas ng listahan ng mga district allocations.

asr-002795
02:46:05.280 --> 02:46:17.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero ang problema nga dun, ito yung nire-raise ni Congressman Chanko, e parang lahat ng so-called allocables ay sa district representative lang.

asr-002796
02:46:18.240 --> 02:46:21.420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam naman natin hindi totoo yun. Kasi yun lang ang makikita mo.

asr-002797
02:46:21.440 --> 02:46:29.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, pag tinignan mo yung GAB, yung General Appropriations Act, not the GAB, you can only see the district, diba?

asr-002798
02:46:30.300 --> 02:46:37.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi mo makikita, katulad ng sinabi niya, paano yung sa party list? Babagsak din naman sa distrito yan, diba?

asr-002799
02:46:37.480 --> 02:46:41.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Paano yung sa senador? Babagsak din sa distrito yan.

asr-002800
02:46:41.400 --> 02:46:49.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kaya po, tama at sinusuportahan natin ang panawagan na ilabas na.

asr-002801
02:46:49.520 --> 02:47:02.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dahil sinabi na rin ni Secretary Bonone, ilabas na yung listahan ng mga proponents, in other words, from 2023 to 2026, and also for 2027.

asr-002802
02:47:03.640 --> 02:47:11.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At dapat hindi malimita sa district representative sa party list, isama din pati mga senador.

asr-002803
02:47:13.480 --> 02:47:19.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam natin na yung mga nakakasuhan ngayon ng plunder na senators, meron pong,

asr-002804
02:47:19.520 --> 02:47:22.000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: senator and former senator, diba?

asr-002805
02:47:22.820 --> 02:47:31.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Na nakasuhan ng plunder, that is on the basis, allegedly, of them being proponents for flood control projects.

asr-002806
02:47:31.960 --> 02:47:37.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero hindi mo makikita yun sa GAA mismo.

asr-002807
02:47:38.440 --> 02:47:48.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kinailangan pang ma-establish through the testimonies of the district engineers, such as Alcantara et al.

asr-002808
02:47:49.520 --> 02:47:59.460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero, sabi nga, in the spirit of reform and transparency, panahon na po para ilabas na ng buo yung listahan ng mga,

asr-002809
02:47:59.460 --> 02:48:12.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and from an official source or official sources, so that would be Congress, Senate, their respective committees on appropriation and finance, as well as the DPWH.

asr-002810
02:48:12.780 --> 02:48:19.460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi pwedeng sabihin ng DPWH na hindi nila alam dahil si Secretary Bonone mismo ang nagsabi sa senador.

asr-002811
02:48:19.520 --> 02:48:20.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sandigan ba yan?

asr-002812
02:48:20.900 --> 02:48:32.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ilabas na po ng buo, alin ang proponent ay senador, alin ang proponent ay district representative, at alin yung sa party list.

asr-002813
02:48:33.000 --> 02:48:34.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For purposes of accountability.

asr-002814
02:48:36.560 --> 02:48:43.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And as I said, dapat, pati sa kasalukuyang budget na tinatalakay natin 2027, moving forward, ganun na rin.

asr-002815
02:48:43.980 --> 02:48:46.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Now, is this unconstitutional?

asr-002816
02:48:47.780 --> 02:48:49.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sasabihin ba na, hindi, bawal yan.

asr-002817
02:48:49.520 --> 02:48:52.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bawal yan sa pork barrel decision, PDAF decision.

asr-002818
02:48:52.820 --> 02:48:53.560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi po bawal.

asr-002819
02:48:54.540 --> 02:48:55.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit hindi?

asr-002820
02:48:55.020 --> 02:49:07.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dahil malinaw naman, ang pinagbawal, ang sinabing unconstitutional ng Bellica v. Ochoa is the post-enactment intervention of legislators during budget execution.

asr-002821
02:49:08.220 --> 02:49:08.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Diba?

asr-002822
02:49:08.860 --> 02:49:17.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung PDAF po kasi, ina-approve lang ng lump sum ng Kongreso, pero yung identification ng project nangyayari during the implementation stage.

asr-002823
02:49:17.780 --> 02:49:19.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun ang sabi ng...

asr-002824
02:49:19.520 --> 02:49:30.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ng Supreme Court na, ano na yan, bawal, violation of separation of powers of the co-equal branches.

asr-002825
02:49:30.280 --> 02:49:48.760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa kaso po, nung kasalukuyang sistema, kaya nga tinanggal na yung PDAF system, post-enactment identification, ina-identify na yung project, either during the budget preparation phase, yung RDC process na sinasabi nyo,

asr-002826
02:49:48.760 --> 02:49:57.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: or during the budget deliberation phase, budget authorization phase, sorry, which is the current process.

asr-002827
02:49:58.360 --> 02:50:00.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, wala pong sabit.

asr-002828
02:50:01.220 --> 02:50:14.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi iligal, hindi unconstitutional, and in the spirit of transparency, dapat na talaga na identified na yung proyekto sa proponent.

asr-002829
02:50:14.640 --> 02:50:18.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kung sinong senador, kung sinong congressman, kung sinong...

asr-002830
02:50:18.760 --> 02:50:24.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: kung sinong party list representative, ma-identify sa project, sasabihin, eh, di EPAL yan, EPAL.

asr-002831
02:50:24.740 --> 02:50:33.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Eh, mas mabuti na po na EPAL, kahit pasabihin mong EPAL, eh, at least may transparency and accountability, diba?

asr-002832
02:50:34.080 --> 02:50:45.560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, cargo na ngayon, nung, kunyari, party list representative, eh, kung palpak talaga yung proyekto, ikaw ang accountable, hindi yung district representative, diba?

asr-002833
02:50:45.560 --> 02:50:45.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ganon?

asr-002834
02:50:46.600 --> 02:50:46.840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-002835
02:50:47.280 --> 02:50:48.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, Mr.

asr-002836
02:50:48.760 --> 02:51:15.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Speaker at ginuong sponsor, sasangayon po ba kayo na magpasok na tayo ng special provision sa general, sa budget ng DPWH that will mandate that proponents, including the legislators, senator, congressman, party list, will be identified, you know, through publication.

asr-002837
02:51:16.780 --> 02:51:18.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, and this will apply...

asr-002838
02:51:18.760 --> 02:51:24.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In the previous budget, for transparency purposes, as well as for the 2027 budget.

asr-002839
02:51:24.620 --> 02:51:25.420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sangayon po kayo doon?

asr-002840
02:51:25.840 --> 02:51:28.520
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: Mr. Speaker, Your Honor, hindi na siguro kailangan ngayon.

asr-002841
02:51:29.120 --> 02:51:32.800
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: Dahil, ah, sa ngayon, wala hong proponent na congressman or senador.

asr-002842
02:51:33.480 --> 02:51:37.480
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: Ang proponent ho ngayon ay ang Department of Public Works and Highways lamang.

asr-002843
02:51:37.940 --> 02:51:41.740
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: In fact, sinabi nga nila, bottoms up nga yung kanilang budgeting.

asr-002844
02:51:41.740 --> 02:51:47.640
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: That it starts from the DEOs to the regional office or up to the central office.

asr-002845
02:51:47.740 --> 02:51:48.740
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: That means...

asr-002846
02:51:48.760 --> 02:51:53.300
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: Those who proposes the projects are the Department of Public Works and Highways themselves.

asr-002847
02:51:53.940 --> 02:52:04.020
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: Kaya nga, mayroon silang RBPs, yung mga regional budget proposals, that passes through this scrutiny of the Provincial Development Council as well as the RDCs.

asr-002848
02:52:04.420 --> 02:52:12.680
Rep. Romeo S. Momo Sr.: Yun po ang pagkakaintindi ko sa budget ngayon under the leadership of Secretary Vins.

asr-002849
02:52:12.680 --> 02:52:16.860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: To wind up, Mr. Speaker, alam kong tapos na ang oras.

asr-002850
02:52:17.780 --> 02:52:18.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well...

asr-002851
02:52:18.760 --> 02:52:22.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, unfortunate po yung sagot ng ating sponsor.

asr-002852
02:52:22.300 --> 02:52:25.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ibig sabihin, hindi siya sang-ayon sa proposal na ito.

asr-002853
02:52:26.300 --> 02:52:35.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, dahil sinasabi niya na, ah, hindi na po nangyayari yung sistema ng, ah, legislators as proponents in the budget.

asr-002854
02:52:35.860 --> 02:52:40.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: This all happens in the, ah, budget preparation phase.

asr-002855
02:52:41.040 --> 02:52:41.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-002856
02:52:42.300 --> 02:52:43.760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dumadaan lahat sa RDC.

asr-002857
02:52:44.440 --> 02:52:44.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-002858
02:52:44.900 --> 02:52:48.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero yung mismong, ah, pag-amin nyo, na meron kayong ihahapit.

asr-002859
02:52:48.760 --> 02:52:51.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kung may ihahabol na 20 billion, akala ko ba dumaan na sa RDC?

asr-002860
02:52:51.660 --> 02:52:53.900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit biglang may ihahabol kayong 20 billion?

asr-002861
02:52:54.840 --> 02:52:56.120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maging tapat po tayo.

asr-002862
02:52:56.320 --> 02:53:02.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung 20 billion na yan, yan yung mga, ah, submissions ng ating mga kongresista.

asr-002863
02:53:02.960 --> 02:53:06.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At pagdating sa Senado, mayroon pa silang ipapasok.

asr-002864
02:53:06.440 --> 02:53:10.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, gawin na pong nating transparent ang prosesong ito.

asr-002865
02:53:10.620 --> 02:53:10.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-002866
02:53:10.700 --> 02:53:19.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, that, ah, call remains at, ah, ah, itutuloy po natin ito hanggang sa, ah, bukas.

asr-002867
02:53:19.800 --> 02:53:25.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang debate, ang open debate in plenary for this 2027 budget.

asr-002868
02:53:26.560 --> 02:53:27.780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maraming salamat po, Mr. Speaker.

asr-002869
02:53:27.780 --> 02:53:31.000
Deputy Speaker Raymond Democrito C. Mendoza: Maraming salamat, Congressman Tino of ACT Teacher.

