Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: But, for example, merong mga ilang kasunduan, such as the Critical Minerals Agreement.

asr-004307
04:14:51.720 --> 04:14:56.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: This is an agreement between, it's not DTI, but the DENR.

asr-004308
04:15:00.000 --> 04:15:13.760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and it's still Jacob Helberg, di ba, of the U.S., the Undersecretary of the State Department of the United States

asr-004309
04:15:13.760 --> 04:15:22.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and considered and recognized as the main proponent of Pax Silica.

asr-004310
04:15:23.420 --> 04:15:26.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, Pebrero pa po pinirmahan to, tama po ba?

asr-004311
04:15:26.940 --> 04:15:40.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Samantala, so in other words, even before the formal signing of the Philippines into the Pax Silica Initiative,

asr-004312
04:15:40.680 --> 04:15:50.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ay pumirman na ng Critical Minerals Agreement ang DENR, at the time it was Secretary Lutilia Steele and Jacob Helberg.

asr-004313
04:15:51.000 --> 04:15:51.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is that correct?

asr-004314
04:15:53.520 --> 04:15:56.160
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleagues, the answer is yes.

asr-004315
04:15:56.160 --> 04:15:56.760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes.

asr-004316
04:15:56.940 --> 04:16:10.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And also, si BCDA Chair or President, sorry, BCDA President Joshua Bingkang,

asr-004317
04:16:11.220 --> 04:16:17.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: nagpadala siya ng sulat sa, again, kay Jacob Helberg,

asr-004318
04:16:17.320 --> 04:16:26.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: containing a proposal for the establishment of a Pax Silica Coordination Office,

asr-004319
04:16:26.940 --> 04:16:36.240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and offering 1,620 hectares of land in New Clark City.

asr-004320
04:16:36.820 --> 04:16:45.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: That letter was dated April, is it April, April 9, tama po ba?

asr-004321
04:16:51.300 --> 04:16:55.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes, April 9, 2026. Is that correct?

asr-004322
04:16:56.940 --> 04:16:57.780
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: Yes.

asr-004323
04:16:59.240 --> 04:17:12.780
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: Mr. Chair, Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleague, the date is correct, but it wasn't just transmitted, it was verbally, it was a note in verbal.

asr-004324
04:17:14.300 --> 04:17:14.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Not verbal?

asr-004325
04:17:14.920 --> 04:17:23.380
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: No, no, no. So, April 9, it wasn't transmitted, but on April 15, it was a note verbally transmitted.

asr-004326
04:17:23.660 --> 04:17:26.380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, point being...

asr-004327
04:17:26.940 --> 04:17:33.700
